## 6) Migration from Firebase to Convex

### **Step 1: Export Firebase Data**
```bash
# Export Firestore data to JSON
gsutil -m cp -r gs://your-project/collections ./firebase-export
```

### **Step 2: Define Convex Schema**
```typescript
// convex/schema.ts
import { defineSchema, defineTable } from "convex/server";
import { v } from "convex/values";

export default defineSchema({
  users: defineTable({
    email: v.string(),
    name: v.string(),
    profile: v.object({
      bio: v.string(),
      avatar: v.string(),
    }),
    createdAt: v.number(),
  })
    .index("by_email", ["email"]),

  messages: defineTable({
    text: v.string(),
    authorId: v.id("users"),
    conversationId: v.id("conversations"),
    timestamp: v.number(),
  })
    .index("by_conversation", ["conversationId"])
    .index("by_author", ["authorId"]),

  conversations: defineTable({
    participantIds: v.array(v.id("users")),
    createdAt: v.number(),
  }),
});
```

### **Step 3: Migrate Data**
```typescript
// convex/migrate.ts
import { internalMutation } from "./_generated/server";
import { v } from "convex/values";

// Run this once to import all Firebase data
export const importFirestoreUsers = internalMutation({
  args: { data: v.array(v.object({ 
    _id: v.string(),
    email: v.string(),
    name: v.string(),
  })) },
  handler: async (ctx, { data }) => {
    for (const user of data) {
      await ctx.db.insert("users", {
        email: user.email,
        name: user.name,
        profile: { bio: "", avatar: "" },
        createdAt: Date.now(),
      });
    }
  },
});
```

**Run migration from dashboard:**
```bash
npx convex run migrate:importFirestoreUsers --args '{"data": [...]}'
```

### **Step 4: Rewrite Client Code**

**Before (Firebase):**
```typescript
import { getFirestore, collection, query, where, onSnapshot } from "firebase/firestore";

const db = getFirestore();
onSnapshot(
  query(collection(db, "messages"), where("conversationId", "==", convId)),
  (snapshot) => {
    setMessages(snapshot.docs.map(d => d.data()));
  }
);
```

**After (Convex):**
```typescript
import { useQuery } from "convex/react";
import { api } from "./convex/_generated/api";

// Automatically reactive!
const messages = useQuery(api.messages.getMessages, { conversationId: convId });
```

### **Step 5: Replace Firebase Rules with Convex Functions**

**Before (Firebase Security Rules):**
```javascript
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /messages/{message} {
      allow read: if request.auth.uid != null;
      allow create: if request.auth.uid == request.resource.data.authorId;
    }
  }
}
```

**After (Convex - Authorization in Code):**
```typescript
export const sendMessage = mutation({
  args: { text: v.string(), conversationId: v.id("conversations") },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    const userId = await ctx.auth.getUserIdentity();
    if (!userId) throw new Error("Not authenticated");

    // Business logic as code
    if (args.text.length > 1000) {
      throw new Error("Message too long");
    }

    return await ctx.db.insert("messages", {
      text: args.text,
      conversationId: args.conversationId,
      authorId: userId.tokenIdentifier,
    });
  },
});
```

### **Migration Complexity Comparison:**

| Aspect | Firebase | Convex |
|--------|----------|--------|
| **Data Export** | Easy (GCP console) | N/A (import to Convex) |
| **Schema Definition** | Implicit (auto from data) | Explicit TypeScript |
| **Code Rewrite** | ~40% (rules → functions) | ~60% (client queries completely different) |
| **Realtime Setup** | Manual `onSnapshot()` | Automatic with hooks |
| **Testing** | Requires emulator | Local dev environment |

